 "Why add instead of replace?": "",
 "The derivative of x + f(x) w.r.t. x includes an identity term ({#}), so the training signal reaches early layers without fading through {#} multiplications (<0>backprop</0>).": "",
 "Why one fixed width?": "",
 "Every sub-layer reads from and writes to the same d_model = {#} space, so all layers \"speak the same language\" and outputs can simply be summed.": "",
 "Logit lens": "",
 "Because the space is shared, you can apply the final norm + unembedding to the stream at any layer and see what it \"would predict\" so far (<0>layer roles</0>).": "",
 "Pre-norm (norm inside the branch, as here) is what Llama-style models use; the original {#} Transformer used post-norm (norm after the add).": "",
