 "RMSNorm(k·x) (gain = {#}) <0/> <1/>": "",
 "rms(input) = {#} → output = input / {#} → rms(output) ≈ {#}": "",
 "Why care? The stream grows as {#} edits pile up. Without a norm, later sub-layers would see ever-larger inputs and training tends to become unstable.": "",
 "RMSNorm rescales a vector so its <0>root-mean-square</0> is {#}, then multiplies each dimension by a learned gain.": "",
 "It keeps the input to each sub-layer at a predictable scale, however big the stream has grown.": "",
 "It works per token: one row at a time, no mixing between tokens.": "",
 "RMSNorm(x) = x / √(mean(x²) + ε) ⊙ g, ε ≈ 1e-5, g ∈ ℝ<0>d_model</0> learned.": "",
 "Unlike LayerNorm it does not subtract the mean and has no bias — cheaper, and works about as well in practice.": "",
